Visit charming Athy in County Kildare and explore old stone castles, relaxing walking trails, and beautiful manors.
Discover the history of the Quakers in Kildare with a visit to Ballitore and Burtown House & Gardens, or take a cruise along the River to see the town from a different angle. Explore ancient heritage sites sprinkled throughout the area such as Kilkea Castle and Whites Castle, which hail from the times of the Normans and Fitzgeralds (the Earls of Kildare), while the 12th century Moate of Ardscull is infamous for legends of the “little people”.
