Brennan’s Kilteel Inn, a 100-year-old Irish pub in the village of Kilteel in County Kildare, has spent lockdown as a film set for a mystery TV series. The pub have been staying tight-lipped on what’s currently being filmed but have been dropping hints that Adrian Dunbar and Tommy Tiernan have both been through the doors recently.
Just 30 minutes from this popular haunt sits the stunning Castletown House; an 18th century Palladian-style country house located in Celbridge, where upcoming Netflix romcom Mr Malcom’s List was recently shot. Famous faces such as Slumdog Millionaire’s Frieda Pinto, Ashely Park of Emily in Paris and heartthrob Theo James from The Divergent Series caused a stir when caught on camera strolling through the Kildare set, where they filmed on location for a number of months.
TwoCooks, a Sallins-based restaurant overlooking The Grand Canal, is coming to the final stages of a large renovation project, which will allow them to better facilitate groups indoors. Nearby neighbours Lock 13 have also carried out significant works to their outdoor dining area.
Burtown House and Gardens is another outdoor dining option in Athy which has seen huge demand upon reopening, with extensive picnic/ takeaway options also available.
Close to Kildare Village, both outdoors dining and the museum at Newbridge Silverware are open to the public with an advance booking not necessary, however, the number of persons admitted is monitored in accordance with the current public health guidelines. Contact info@intokildare.ie for any membership related queries.
