]]> Let the Gordon Bennett Driving Route take you on an historic journey across spectacular Irish countryside and into the picturesque towns and villages of county Kildare in the heart of Ireland.
Across the water you will be struck by the imposing Leixlip Castle which has parts dating back 1172 and the time of the Norman invasions. This building provides the strongest living link to Arthur as it was purchased by his descendant Desmond Guinness in 1958.
Your last stop on the trail will take you to Oughterard Cemetery, the final resting place of Arthur Guinness and some of his family members. The graveyard is set atop a small hill and gives awe-inspiring views of Kildare s sweeping landscape and to the South the Dublin and Wicklow mountains.
