Not To Be Missed, Stay, BargeTrip, Canals, Kildare, Lough 13, Sallins, Tourism, Naas
Wake up to the sounds of lapping water or eat al fresco on the deck, as you see the countryside from a canal or barge. BargeTrip.ie in Sallins, Co Kildare have just announced a new overnight package and we couldn’t be more excited.
“Staying overnight on a barge is just like a night in an apartment and as well as stopping off for a tipple along the way, you’ve your own bar on board. There’s room for up to six people on the overnight barge and as a destination, Sallins has it all.
One of the stops along the way is Lough 13, a local pub on the Grand Canal in Sallins which is a firm favourite of Ger’s – not only do they brew their own beer but they have a tasty menu to go with it.
Barge trips down the canal are just as popular with the locals as they are with visitors and tickets are now available in the tourist office in Dublin.
Crawling along at 5km p/h, sipping a glass of locally brewed beer, it’s hard to imagine the thousands of boats and lives that occupied these canals right up until the 1960s.
For beer fanatics, you won’t be disappointed with a vibrant craft beer scene to sample and for cocktail lovers, many bars and restaurants have specially trained mixologists. Or perhaps you prefer to relax in front of an open fire in a traditional pub with a glass of the black stuff, we are the home of Arthur after all!
Located in the heart of Naas Co. Kildare and open 7 days a week serving great food, cocktails, events and live music.
The ultimate destination venue. You can literally EAT, DRINK, DANCE, SLEEP on-site which has become the motto for this iconic pub.
