Visit Newbridge Silverware Visitor Centre – home to the Museum of Style Icons one of the most unique collections of fashion and cinema memorabilia in the world
Castletown House is Ireland’s largest and earliest Palladian style house. Built between 1722 and 1729 for William Conolly Speaker of the Irish House of Commons and the wealthiest commoner in Ireland.
