Autumn has officially landed in Ireland, and with it, brings a crimson carpet of foliage and a chill to the air.
The warm autumnal palette of misty yellows and auburn tones are filling everyone’s Instagram feeds of late. Here at Into Kildare, we asked the people of the Thoroughbred County to share their best autumn pictures.
Why not spend some quality family time outdoors in Kildare this mid-term break, and discover all the wonders Kildare’s countryside has to offer. Thanks to the Irish Explorers for sending this picture our way.
Photographer Aimee McCormack managed to capture the entire colour scheme of autumn in one shot, while visiting the breathtaking Castletown House. This historical house was built in 1720s, and is the perfect place to spend the day with family, exploring the parkland and river walks of the area.
Thanks to Norma Thiessen, a visitor from Ontario, Canada for this shot of the stunning Japanese Gardens of the National Stud Farm. The Stud provides the perfect day out for families, filled with activities for all to enjoy, like the playground and kids zone, museum, gardens, tours and on-site restaurant.
