After a busy day of uncovering the myths and legends of Kildare’s heritage sites, or the exhilaration of a day at the races, or dancing the night away at an impromptu traditional music session, you’ll need a good night’s rest. So where do you want to lay your head, get a great sleep and begin the next day of your adventure on your holiday?
Explore Parallel Tales of Wealth and Destitution - IntoKildare
Explore some of Waterford city’s most significant artefacts and historic tales at Bishop’s Palace, the Georgian mansion and museum.
Rebuilt in the early 18th century, this beautiful country house is called home by the MacMurrough Kavanaghs, former High Kings of Leinster. Dermot MacMurrough may have gotten more than he bargained for when he invited the Normans to Ireland in 1167, but today his legacy lives on in the splendid form of this enchanting mansion and its grounds.Another of Ireland’s hidden gems can be found a short drive away in the lush countryside of County Carlow.
Within its walls were thousands of prisoners during the Great Famine, the 1798 Rebellion and the War of Independence. Today, you can explore the chilling tales and ominous dungeon corridors of this historic site in the company of a troupe of local actors – while more daring visitors can book ahead for the paranormal tour.
Journey Overview At the heart of the Boyne Valley’s luxuriant green countryside, Beaulieu House and Garden stands as a beautifully preserved icon of another age.
On your next stop, it’s a captivating vista that meets the eye at Carrickmacross Workhouse in County Monaghan. Erected in the 1840s and later the site of a much-needed fever hospital, this historic building now stands as a versatile heritage centre, organised by local volunteers.
Ask a Local: Where to Bring Visitors in Kildare?
Families, Adventure Seekers, Outdoor Enthusiasts, Things To Do
If you’ve been holding off on a family staycation until the later part of the year and you’re looking for a break that ticks all the boxes in terms of accommodation, fun activities and being able to explore the outdoors – Kildare has got all of them in abundance.
If you’re looking for the full rural countryside farm experience – why not opt for staying in a real life farm. Ballindrum Farm is a fully operational dairy farm ( you can get tours if you book in advance) but also has four star self -catering accommodation available.
Athy Boat Tours is just one option in close proximity if you’ve got some water babies who love getting out amongst nature and wildlife.
Complimentary bikes are also available to all guests so you can have a leisurely cycle through the picturesque estate.
For creative fairies, Florence and Milly is located close by and offers ceramics, painting and pottery classes.
With award winning gardens and top- class health and leisure facilities – it’s a perfect family option for a hotel break. If you’ve got a few minutes of free time to spare – the spa is also highly recommended.
In the heart of Maynooth, the Glenroyal Hotel offers some brilliant family friendly facilities from huge family rooms to a swimming pool.
Food & Drink, Accommodation, Couples, Things To Do
Treat your someone special to a romantic meal for two with a glass of bubbly for €70, followed by a romantic walk through the woodlands and gardens. Find the love swing, butterfly gardens & fountains on your stroll, or why not book in for a luxury treatment in the spa.
Enjoy a little romance with a beautiful one-night getaway with Prosecco & CLIFF chocolates waiting in your room on arrival.
Complete your stay with a delicious full Irish breakfast the next morning before strolling hand in hand through the crackling leaves or even make use of the complimentary CLIFF bikes and cycle down along the canal. For more information,click here.
Love is in the at at the Keadeen this Valentine’s. The team at the Keadeen want to make sure you and your loved one enjoy and evening to remember, so Executive Head Chef Kevin Curran has created a delectable and lovingly prepared menu for this very special evening.
Want to celebrate Valentine’s Day in style this year?
One or two night packages are available, including a choice of Castle or Carriage accommodation with a glass of bubbly for the both of you and chocolates upon arrival.
Carriage Bedroom Experience – €495 for a 2-night stay Castle Bedroom Experience – €695 for a two-night stay.
Lounge around in your spacious room in complementary fluffy bathrobes and slippers, and afterward enjoy a three-course meal at Herald & Devoy restaurant.
There will also be a live pianist in Osprey Bar on the evening of the 14th February.
For something extra special, couples can choose to enjoy a picnic hand prepared by the Carton House team of chefs by theBoat House, a relaxing treatment inCarton House Spaor a delicious serving ofafternoon teain the original Stewarts Kitchen of Carton House. Contact the teamherefor more information.
Love is in the air in Clandard Court this Valentine’s Day with a special V-Day menu served exclusively for three nights on Thursday 14th, Friday 15th and Saturday 16th February.
A complimentary room upgrade makes your stay in one of the luxurious bedrooms that much nicer while champagne and chocolates on arrival add that delightful extra touch. Enjoy an exquisite four-course dining experience in the Byerley Turk Restaurant which offers the perfect romantic atmosphere to make the night truly special.
Barberstown Castle has been a special part of couple’s lives since the Middle Ages. Create your own memories of this unique haven with food that is prepared with a passion by Master Chef Bertrand Malabat.
From just €179 per person sharing, enjoy a romantic break away at the Court Yard Hotel, complete with a dreamy candle-lit dinner for two and a glass of prosecco to toast your love.
Best Places in Kildare for an Epic Lads Getaway - IntoKildare
It’s hard to beat a good bro-mance and let’s not forget, it is just as important for lads to spend time with their male friends so that they can relax, unwind and bond. There are plenty of great experiences in Kildare that are perfect for an adventure filled and sophisticated lad’s weekend.
All aboard, while you charter a private cruise for you and your mates!
Adrenaline junkies who want to test your skills and energy levels to the limit, then check out Redhills Adventure Centre.
If all of that activity has worked up an appetite, the boys will enjoy a leisurely lunch at the original site where Arthur Guinness created his brewing empire in ‘Arthur’s Bar’ at the Court Yard Hotel, Leixlip. Whilst enjoying lunch you and the boys can catch up on all the latest sporting fixtures on their giant outdoor screen!
Clane, Families, Couples, Hidden Gems, Things To Do, Accommodation
If you’re looking for an accommodation option suitable for a group of people, Robertstown Holiday Village is a great option which is only a 15 minute drive away. The self catering cottages are in a stunning location over looking the Grand Canal which truly enhances your rural Irish experience.
Lullymore Heritage and Discovery Park , an award winning day visitor attraction perfect for all ages. All visitors have the freedom to explore the natural wonders of Lullymore along vast trails in serene ancient woodland and on the peatland biodiversity boardwalk.
If you’re a fan of art, Kilcock Art Gallery is close by and well worth a visit to marvel at the exhibitions and art pieces.
The River Liffey runs straight through Clane and makes for a lovely, tranquil walk on the waterside.
Four-star self-catering accommodation in a great location for exploring the surrounding areas.
Butt Mullins is a family run business known for their warm customer service and attention to detail for over 30 years.
Mouth watering menus prepared by top chefs, served in a stylish and relaxed setting by a team who really cares. Athy
The Irish Restaurant Awards showcase the true talent that Ireland’s hospitality industry has to offer!
The public chose their favourites across 21 categories including Best Restaurant, Best Casual Dining, Best Chef, Best Seafood Experience, Best World Cuisine and more.
We had some very worthy winners on the night, and Into Kildare would like to wish them a huge congratulations!
