Non-alloy steel Carbon content is less than 0.8%, only Fe but no other alloying elements
Low-alloy steel Alloying elements are less than or equal to 5%
High alloy steel Alloying elements higher than 5%
In the scope of metal cutting, the P group is the largest material group because it covers several different industrial fields. The material is usually a long material, which can be machined continuously and relatively uniformly.
- The cutting force and power required to process ISO P materials are within a limited range.
- Good metal cutting control under all working conditions.
- Contains non-ferrous metals, soft metals with hardness less than 130 HB.
Aircraft manufacturing industry and aluminum alloy car wheel manufacturers occupy a dominant position in Group N.
- The cutting force and power required to process ISO N materials are within a limited range.
- Metal cutting control under is relatively difficult.
The hardened steels in Group H are used in various industries, such as the automotive industry and its subcontractors, as well as machine manufacturing and mold business.
- High cutting force and power required.
