The best alternatives to Paypal with hardly any commissions
In PayPal we have some commissions in some operations, something that is annoying for many users. Therefore, it may be interesting to know some of the main alternatives to PayPal that we have available at present, since in many of them there are fewer commissions or there are hardly any commissions.
One of the advantages of using this method is that no additional commissions.
Google Pay is a particularly secure option, but it's easy to use every time. The fact that we can use it in online purchases (more and more pages support this option), so we can use it in these purchases.
Apple Pay is another option that can be seen as one of the best alternatives to PayPal what is on the market. In this case, it is associated with your Apple account and you will be able to make online payments using this payment method.
It is another good option if you were looking for alternatives to PayPal. Apple Pay is easy to use, is a payment method that we can use in many cases, since there are many web pages that support it, in addition to being able to use it in physical stores, which makes it so comfortable.
Bizum If what really interests us is the option to send money to friends or family, or receive it, then Bizum is an ideal app for it.
Bizum has the advantage that it works immediately.
It is an app that millions of people use in Spain, so it is the most comfortable when what you are interested in is sending or receiving money. In addition, the use of Bizum does not incur additional costs, which is another aspect that has helped make it so popular.
This app is another alternative to PayPal in the field of sending money to friends or family.
Inside the application we have a wallet and we can invite other users, contacts, to send them money then. It is also ideal when going out with friends, because you can create groups where you can create a common boat for that dinner or that night.
Developer: Verse Technologies
Twyp is an option that stands out for allowing you to send international transfers, its free API to manage payments in stores, it gives you access to a Mastercard card and It has very low commissions. Therefore, there are not going to be excessive costs, something that was precisely being sought in this case, since we want alternatives to PayPal with low commissions.
