Windows libraries are files that are used by certain applications and are installed natively on the system. This way, games that want to make use of those libraries don't have to include the files in the installation package.
If the app or game you want to run does not include this set of apps, you will never be able to run it. If that set of apps is old, Windows won't let you run the game or app either.
