Let’s see below what steps to follow in each of the cases:
To do this, we will first go to "Settings".
Perfect then. If not, obviously, it will have to be activated, because we will need it to locate our mobile in case of theft or loss.
What we must do is then is to make use of a computer in which we have logged in to Google (we can check it in the upper right corner of the screen), enter google and write in the search box this phrase: «Where is my phone". As simple as that.
After clicking “Search” or pressing the Enter key, a module will appear on the screen from which to access the device location map, as shown in the image above, and two options below:
To recover.
On the other hand, the «Retrieve» option, or the option to click on the map module, takes us to the GoogleAndroidFind, which shows the map with the most recent location of our device. In the left column of the map there are several security options available, such as to block to sign out of the Google account or delete the data, so that the possible thief cannot obtain any sensitive information stored on our phone.
The method to locate an iPhone is even simpler than in the case of an Android mobile. Actually, all you have to do is enter the "Search" application which is already pre-installed on the device.
After pressing the button, we will jump to a new screen in which a map with exact location of all Apple devices associated with our user profile. Once the one we are looking for is located (as in the example shown in the image above), we must click on it again to see the Options:
Activate "Lost Mode", which automatically locks all phone functions.
These are the two methods, for Android and for iOS, to locate a lost or stolen phone. It only remains to insist that, in order to be completely calm and know that there will be a remedy for these cases, it is of the utmost importance to make sure that we have activated the corresponding option to share location or location.
