Many people also like to wash their hands with foam soap, because the foam soap is so good that it is easy to wash off from the hands. Liquid soap can be very sticky, which makes it take longer to wash off your hands.
Before making your own foam soap, be sure to buy a highly rated foam soap dispenser like Amazon. These dispensers have a special air chamber that pumps air into the soap when the soap is released.
The first step in how to make foaming soap is to add water to the foaming soap dispenser. You should fill the water dispenser with approximately two-thirds to three-quarters of water.
To make a foaming hand sanitizer, first add 2 tablespoons of castile soap to the water in the dispenser (this soap is suitable for a 12-ounce soap dispenser). Castile soap is naturally biodegradable and non-toxic, making it an excellent choice for making your own foaming hand sanitizer.
When deciding which essential oil to add, there are many different options to consider. You can choose essential oils based on their smell, or choose essential oils with antibacterial properties, such as tea tree oil, eucalyptus oil, or lemongrass oil.
When you plan your foaming hand sanitizer formula, don’t forget to add a carrier oil to the mixture. Carrier oils, such as jojoba oil, coconut oil, olive oil or sweet almond oil, can help your foaming soap be more moisturized, which is especially beneficial in cold and dry winters.
