You know the feeling: very familiar muscle soreness after exercise.
This painful but strange reward sensation in the muscles is called delayed muscular syndrome or DOMS, and it can reasonably slow you down. A 2012 study pointed out: “DOMS can cause reductions in joint range of motion, shock absorption, and peak torque, thereby affecting athletic performance.” The tendons are under unaccustomed pressure”.
“Although vibration therapy feels good on the surface of the body, it is a “global” experience rather than a targeted experience. Impact therapy targets the treatment by going deep into the muscles to increase the blood flow and oxygen required for effective treatment and recovery.
The most significant differences can be found in build quality and two key performance statistics called stall force and amplitude. The stall force is the amount of pressure the gun needs to stop applying vertical force to the muscles.
