Peter’s words pierced their hearts, and they said to him and to the other apostles, “Brothers, what should we do?” (Acts 2:36, 37 NLT)
You see, because of Jesus’ sacrifice, everybody is going to get saved. Just relax and go home.”
Let us say that a person has defrauded you of some money. If they won’t acknowledge the wrongdoing, if they won’t ask you to forgive them, then you are under no obligation to do so.
However, granting forgiveness when there is no repentance is also unloving as we could just be enabling the person to continue to engage in wrongdoing. The Bible warns us, “When the sentence for a crime is not speedily executed, the hearts of men become fully set on doing evil.” (Ecclesiastes 8:11 BSB)
