James 2:13 answers the question. He says:
To illustrate how this works, Jesus uses a term that has to do with accounting.
In the time of Jesus, a rich man might hire trumpeters to walk in front of him as he carried his gift offering to the temple. People would hear the sound and come out of their homes to see what was going on, to see him strolling by, and they would think what a wonderful and generous man he is.
He also says at Matthew 12:43-45 that when the spirit is not in a man, his house is empty and soon seven wicked spirits will take it over and his situation will be worse than before. Then the apostle Paul tells us at 2 Corinthians 11:13-15 that there will be ministers who pretend to be righteous but are really guided by the spirit of Satan.
