Description: Many processes such as PCB manufacturing, PCB assembly, and testing require accurate positioning of the PCB. Therefore, it is generally required to design positioning holes.
(1)For each PCB, at least two positioning holes should be designed, one is circular and the other is long groove shape, the former is used for positioning and the latter is used for guiding.
Locating holes shall be non metallized. If the PCB is a blanking PCB, the hole plate should be designed for positioning hole to enhance rigidity.
The center of the positioning hole should be more than 5.0 mm away from the transmission side, and the two positioning holes should be as far away as possible. It is recommended to lay them at the diagonal of the PCB.
(4) In addition to three optical positioning fiducial for the whole plate, it is better to design two or three optical positioning fiducial at the corners of each unit plate.
(6) If there are mounting components on both sides, there should be optical positioning fiducial on each side.
