The essential elements of the hydraulic operation process of the three-beam and four-column hydraulic press have been known for a long time:
The hydraulic press can detect force, adjustability of speed and stroke, and operate reliability. If a problem is found, it should be corrected in time.
For the hydraulic system, the working parameters of each working cycle and the various actions that constitute the cycle, such as force, speed, acceleration, starting and ending points of the stroke, time for each action, and the total time of the entire cycle, etc. Adjusting to the correct value can make the system obtain a correct and reliable working cycle.
Personnel who do not understand the structural performance or operating procedures of the hydraulic press are not allowed to start the machine without authorization; during the operation of the four-column hydraulic press, the machine should not be inspected and adjusted; when the four-column hydraulic press finds serious oil leakage or other abnormal conditions (such as unreliable operation, noise, etc.) Vibration, etc.
Do not overload or exceed the eccentricity of the four-column hydraulic press, and do not exceed the stroke of the slider. A warm reminder from the manufacturers of three-beam and four-column hydraulic presses, the clamping height should not be less than 600mm.
It can be used for sheet metal parts of the stretch forming, turning, bending and stamping process, and can also be used for general pressing process according to the user’s needs to increase punching buffer, punching, mobile workbench and other devices. In addition to being used for forging and pressing, the three beam and four column hydraulic press can also be used for rectification, pressing, packing, pressing blocks and plates, etc.
