Problems and solutions that easily occur in the SMC molding process News
The problems that are likely to occur in the SMC molding process are: blistering and internal bulging on the surface of the product; warpage and deformation of the product; cracks in the product after a period of time, and partial fiber exposure of the product. The reasons for the related phenomena and the disposal measures are as follows:
This phenomenon may be caused by incomplete curing of FRP/SMC, low molding temperature and insufficient holding time; uneven thickness of the product, resulting in uneven shrinkage.
The structure of the inserts in the product is unreasonable; the number of inserts is too much; the demoulding method is unreasonable, and the thickness of each part of the product is too different. The solution is to change the structure of the product under permitted conditions, and the insert must meet the requirements of molding; reasonably design the demoulding mechanism to ensure the average ejection force.
The solution is to strictly control the molding temperature, pressure and press timing; ensure sufficient materials and no shortage of materials.
The reason for this phenomenon may be unreasonable mold design; too much material added, etc. The solution is to carry out a reasonable mold design; strictly control the feeding amount.
The problems of products during the molding process are not limited to the above. In the production process, sum up experience, continuous improvement, and improve quality.
