Servo hydraulic press is suitable for stretching, bending, flanging, cold extrusion, blanking and other processes of metal materials, and is suitable for correcting press-fitting, pressing of powder products, abrasive products, and press-forming of plastic products and insulating materials. Where can the precision control and advantages of the servo hydraulic press be reflected?
This new type of servo-driven hydraulic press (servo hydraulic press for short) is an energy-saving and high-efficiency hydraulic press that uses a servo motor to drive the main drive oil pump, reduces the control valve loop, and controls the hydraulic press slider. It is suitable for stamping, die forging, press-fitting, straightening and other processes.
1. Less heat and cost reduction: The hydraulic oil consumed by servo-driven hydraulic presses is generally only about 50% of that of traditional hydraulic presses
High degree of automation, good flexibility and high precision: The pressure, speed and position of the servo-driven hydraulic press are fully closed-loop digital control, with high degree of automation and good precision. In addition, its pressure and speed are programmable to meet the needs of various processes, and it can also realize remote automatic control.
Energy saving: Compared with traditional hydraulic machines, servo-driven hydraulic machines can save electricity by 30%~70%.
Low noise: The noise of the servo hydraulic press is generally less than 70dB, while the noise of the traditional hydraulic press is 83dB~90dB.
High efficiency: The speed of the servo-controlled hydraulic press can be greatly increased, and the working cycle is several times higher than that of the traditional hydraulic press, which can reach 10/min~15/min.
