Therefore the chances of employment in Japanese companies in Cambodia are also high. Taking this opportunity, Japanese Business Association in Cambodia, Japanese Department at Royal University of Phnom Penh and Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center (CJCC) will co-organize an event “Japanese Companies Job Fair”.
At the same time, there will be interviews between Japanese companies and Cambodian participants who wish to apply to companies they are interested in as well. Moreover, there will be presentations from Japanese companies in CJCC seminar rooms to introduce their companies and recruitment process to all participants.
(for detail of CJCC project please click here ⇒ ) CJCC is managed by the cooperation between the Government of Cambodia and Japan under the technical cooperation project through the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) “Project Phase 1-April 2004-March 2009, Project Phase 2-April 2009-March 2014”.
