One of the keys when we play Pokémon is to know more about the types of Poké ball that we meet available in it. It is one of those aspects that can make a difference as we progress through the game and that will help us to be winners.
The usual thing is that these types of Poké Ball can be divided into different groups or categories, so that it is much easier to know what we are in this universe. These categories indicate the functionality of each of these types, because there are Poké balls that will be used in specific situations or that will work with specific types of Pokémon, for example.
3 Poké Ball for specific purposes
The first category that we find is that of the classics, that is to say, those that we find from the first generation of this Pokémon universe. They are the most essential and that we are going to find at all times or that we will use them in any of the games in this world.
Superball: It is similar to the previous one, although it has somewhat better capture probabilities, ideal with those Pokémon that are somewhat more complex to capture. It comes out in stores when we have obtained the Plant Medal in Pueblo Hoyuelo.
The bad news is that there is only one in the entire game, which we can obtain when we have completed the main story. The recommendation is to use this type of Poké ball against Zacian and Zamazenta.
The second category that we find in the game Poké Balls can be considered for the various types of Pokémon that we meet in the various games. That is, there are types of Poké Ball that will work better with a specific type of Pokémon that comes our way.
Bait Ball: This type of Poké Ball works best with those Pokémon caught with the pole. In addition, Bolifacio is going to give it to us in the lobby of the Pueblo Amura Stadium.
Mesh Ball: This type will work best with either Water-type or Bug-type Pokémon. It can be purchased at the Pokémon Center in the lower area of Piston Town.
Ball Weight: It is a very specific type, which will work better with those Pokémon that are very heavy. Bolifacio in the lobby of the Pueblo Ladera Stadium is going to give us this specific type.
Ball Gathering: It is a type of Poké Ball that is going to work with those Pokémon that you have already caught at least once before. It can be purchased at the main Pokémon Center in Topo City.
Love Ball: It is a category that will work with Pokémon of the same species but of the opposite sex to the one we already have today. Bolifacio is going to give it to us in the lobby of the Pueblo Plié Stadium.
It can be purchased from the main Pokémon Center in Topo City. In addition, it is common for the employee of the Rotocrono League in the Wild Area to have it for sale when we meet in that place.
Turn Ball: This type will allow us to improve its capture probability as more turns of combat pass in the game. We can buy it at the main Pokémon Center in Artejo City.
