This is done by reviewing the photocopy, comparing it with the original document, in order to see that it is identical, that there are no changes or manipulations in it. If this is the case, said photocopy is certified by means of a seal or some distinction, which depends on the protocol, which will demonstrate its validity.
A quality photocopy of the original document: Quality means that everything must be clearly read in it, to see that nothing has been modified or falsified in said document or documents that we are going to deliver.
Identification: A DNI, NIE, driver's license or passport or something that serves to identify said person who has to deliver this certified document in any instance, body or administration.
Where can it be done
