Each of them has its own characteristics, in addition to being more useful to be used with certain Pokémon, for example. We tell you more about each of them, as well as the ways in which we can achieve them when we are playing.
Pokeball: It is the classic, the one of all the life. It is the one they give us at the beginning of the adventure and we can buy it in all the Pokémon Center stores by talking to the seller.
ultra-ball: It is an even more effective option than the previous ones, perfect for those Pokémon that are complex to capture as we advance in the world. When we have obtained the Fairy Medal in Plié Town, it will begin to appear in stores.
Diving Ball: This particular type works best with Pokémon that live in areas of water. It can be purchased at the main Pokémon Center in Artejo City, and the Rotochron League employee in the Wild Area usually has it for sale as well.
Dream Ball: This is a type that works best with those Pokémon that are asleep when we find them in the game. Bolifacio in the lobby of the Ciudad Puntera Stadium is going to give it to us.
Moonball: This is a type that works best with Pokémon that can evolve with the Moonstone. Again, Bolifacio is going to give it to us, in this case in the lobby of the Pueblo Auriga Stadium.
We will be able to buy it at the Pokémon Center in the lower area of Piston City. As in other cases, it is for sale from the Rotocrono League employee, in the Wild Area.
Nightfall Ball: This Poké Ball is a type that will be best at night and with Pokémon that live in dark areas in the game universe. It can be purchased at the main Pokémon Center in Artejo City.
Quickball: The last one in this category works best with Pokémon that are very fast and therefore somewhat complex to capture. Obtained as a reward for completing 11 circuits of the Rotochron in the Wilderness Area.
Not only are there types of Poké Balls for certain types of Pokémon, but there are we also have them for effects or situations determined. This may mean that they are specific models to capture a Pokémon that we already have, or that it is of the same species, but of a different sex, for example.
Friend Ball: Its main function or characteristic is that it instantly increases the friendship you have with the Pokémon trapped at that moment. Bolifacio in the lobby of the Pueblo Hoyuelo Stadium is going to give it to us.
Honor Ball: This specific type is just as effective as a basic Poké Ball, the classic of all life. We will get it for every time we buy 10 normal Poké Balls in any store.
Healthy Ball: This specific type has the ability to restore HP and PP and also heals the status problems of the trapped Pokémon. It can be purchased at the Pokémon Center in the lower area of Piston Town.
Speed Ball: It is a specific type that will work better when we have to capture a Pokémon in the first turn of the fight. It is available for sale at the main Pokémon Center in Leading Town.
