Those who play Pokémon with a certain frequency will surely know the term Natures in the game. This concept is very important when we play, because it is something that influences our Pokémon.
4 Natures and food
This attribute reflects individual personality from each of them. This means that even though two different Pokémon belong to the same species, they can have natures that are totally different.
This is especially true in the case of the mother, whose nature they inherit as long as the mother wears an eternal stone equipped. So it is a way of making sure that some of the individuals have a certain nature in the game.
The various Pokémon in the game can only belong to one of these natures. So it is not that we are going to find one that mixes several of them (at least not at the moment).
Huraña (Lonely): favors attack and impairs defense.
Meek (Quiet): favors the special attack and impairs speed.
Fearful (Timid): favors speed and impairs attack.
Rogue (Naughty): favors attack but impairs special defense.
As we have said before, on your Pokémon's status screen you will be able to see the nature it has, either in Spanish or in English. This way you will be able to know more about the way in which said individual will act or how it will affect their various characteristics as the game progresses.
In the most recent editions of the game you can see now which statistics go up and which ones go down as a consequence of its nature. The stat that is benefiting by its nature and that is going to grow is normally displayed in a reddish color, while the one that is going to decrease is shown in blue.
If a Pokémon likes the taste of a specific food, this will have an effect on its contest stats or affection level. This is something that also has an effect in the opposite case, if there is some food whose taste you do not like at all.
Mints can be purchased at the counter on the left. We have to pay 50 battle points for them.
Coarse Mint:Increase special defense and decrease speed.
