Thanks to this you can better advance in Pokémon, by being aware of what this term implies in the game. In addition, we tell you more about all of them and the best way to master them all when you are playing on your account in the popular title.
Natures are something that can be check on status screen of each of the beasts. Also, it is good to know that these natures are something that influence all the characteristics of said individual (Attack, Special Attack, Speed, Defense, Special Defense and Health Points).
Crazy (Rash): favors the special attack and impairs the special defense.
Gentle: favors the special defense, but impairs the defense.
Cautious (Careful): favors the special defense but impairs the special attack.
Firm (Adamant): favors the attack but impairs the special attack.
Strong (Hardy): Neutral.
Rude or Rogue (Sassy): favors attack but impairs special defense.
But this is something that also depends on the nature in question, because there are some that are neutral, that have no effect on its characteristics, so they will not produce changes in the evolution they have. The increase of a statistic is usually 10%, as well as its decrease, in the case of those characteristics that are negatively affected by nature.
Natures like Strong, Tame, Rare, or Serious are neutral, so they will not influence the characteristics of any of your Pokémon. The rest of the 25 that we have mentioned in the previous section have influence, both positive and negative, but this is something that you will be able to see for yourself in the state of your beasts in the game.
This is something that is usually indicated in the form of a preference for a certain flavor in pokécubos, pokochos, or malasadas. In addition, this also affects the effect that certain berries have on Pokémon, so that they can make there are flavors that they like more or that there are others that they do not want, as well as the way in which those berries can affect them.
These combinations are something that we will learn as we advance in the game. The first time it can be confusing, but as we feed them we can see the affection that certain foods have in the game depending on their nature.
To get those Battle Points to pay for the mints with, we will have to participate in combats. This is something that we can do in this Battle Tower, so that it will be simple to be able to obtain those points and later buy these mints that we can use in our Pokémon.
Pokémon has introduced 21 different types of Mints, which will generate a certain effect. They are all these:
Friendly Mint: Increase special defense but decrease defense.
Rogue Mint:Increase Attack and Decrease Special Defense.
Serena Mint:Increase special defense and decrease attack.
